  "contracts": [
    "AC1: Proposed success response: HTTP 200 with JSON { status: 'healthy', version: string, environment: 'production' | 'preview' | 'development' | 'test' | 'unknown', timestamp: string }. timestamp is generated per request as UTC ISO 8601.",
    "AC2: Availability initially means the application status endpoint responds successfully. Supabase readiness, latency metrics and degraded/503 responses require a separately agreed dependency-check design.",
    "AC3: version comes from the application package.json version through a server-side import. Do not depend on npm_package_version being present in deployed processes.",
    "AC4: Recognized VERCEL_ENV values take precedence; otherwise normalize NODE_ENV. Unsupported or missing values become 'unknown'. Expose only the agreed response fields.",
    "AC5: Return Cache-Control: no-store; frontend fetches with cache: 'no-store'. The installed Next.js guide states Route Handlers are uncached by default.",
    "AC6: /api/status is accessible without authentication or Supabase configuration and does not invoke session refresh. Exact status-route exemptions must preserve authorization handling for existing protected routes.",
    "AC7: Frontend request failures display unavailable or unknown state with retry; unavailable version/environment values must not be fabricated.",
    "File ownership must remain disjoint. A single coordinator owns verification commands and .next/ usage. Existing untracked .orchestrator/features/ artifacts remain untouched."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "lib/supabase/proxy.ts:70 calls auth.getUser before checking whether a route is protected. Adding a public endpoint alone would retain an unintended Supabase dependency.",
